Z||000000||Frank Sombers||01-27-2001||08:31 PM||||Are the dogbones from different year 4 cylinder Fieros interchangeable? I would like to get poly bushings for an '84 dogbone and use this in my '88 cpe. This way I'll have poly bushings without needing to buy the ultimate dogbone as I want to retain more of a "stock" look. Thanks to everyone for your time and opinions.<BR>Frank||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||01-27-2001||08:58 PM||||<BR>I believe that all 4-cylinder dog bones interchange.  And, I believe it is possible to purchase poly bushings to place in a 4-cyl dog bone - available from the fierostore.<BR><P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)<BR>Please visit my <A HREF="http://www.trifocus.net/~fws/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Work Shop</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||01-28-2001||03:29 PM||||All 4 cyl struts are the same length. Polly only fits the older style strut. there is an article about struts and 4 cyl in my cave. <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Fiero Cave</A><P>Before replacing a strut make sure all other mounts are good.||||reg||1
